  produces, and it's a security-shaped bug, since "app thinks you're logged in" is exactly the state you don't want
  wrong. Logout and clearing are also the cheapest to build while the module is being written and awkward to retrofit
  once forms depend on it. I'd skip the second consumer; the interface is small enough to get right without one.

